{STRATEGY_GEN_NightMomentum}
{v2.3: Pure Night Strategy with Robust Daily 05:00 Flat (PRIMARY SAFETY)}
{Category A: Night Session Opening Range Breakout}
{Direction: Long Only (Short removed: MC12 Short PF=0.93)}
{Timeframe: 15-min on TXF1}

{ v2.3 CHANGELOG (2026-06-13):

  DESIGN PHILOSOPHY CORRECTION:
    v2.2 framed the fix as "Holiday Module + ExitTime bug fix",
    which mis-prioritized the fundamental requirement.

    For a PURE NIGHT strategy, the CORE requirement is:
    "Position MUST be 0 at 05:00 night session close, EVERY
    NIGHT, regardless of whether next day is a holiday."

    v2.3 makes this explicit by:
    1. PRIMARY safety = DailyFlat mechanism (every night)
    2. SECONDARY safety = Holiday module (for documentation
       and edge cases; mostly redundant for S1)
    3. TERTIARY safety = Day Session Emergency (catches any
       position that somehow survived to 08:45+)

  ARCHITECTURE CHANGES:
    Renamed input ExitTime -> split into 3 dedicated inputs:
      EntryEnd_Time(415)        : entries BLOCKED at Time >= this
      DailyFlat_Time(415)       : forced flat fires from Time >= this
      NightCloseBar_Time(500)   : DO NOT fire on this bar
                                  (= 04:45-05:00 last night bar;
                                   firing here = 08:45 day-open
                                   gap = bug)

    Renamed label LX_NM_Time -> LX_NM_DailyFlat (clearer intent)

    Added new label LX_NM_DaySession_EMERGENCY:
      Catches positions that somehow survived to day session
      (08:45-13:45). Should NEVER fire if DailyFlat works -
      investigate immediately if it does.

  GUARANTEED FLAT-BY-05:00 LOGIC:
    With defaults (DailyFlat_Time=415, NightCloseBar_Time=500):
      Time=415 (04:00-04:15 close) fires sell next bar at market
        -> fills at OPEN of Time=430 bar (04:15)
      Time=430 (retry) -> fills at 04:30
      Time=445 (retry) -> fills at 04:45 OPEN of Time=500 (last night bar)
      Time=500 (NightCloseBar) -> NEVER FIRES (would cause 08:45 gap)

    Position GUARANTEED flat by 04:45 OPEN (one bar before close).
    3 retry chances provide robustness against transient fill issues.

  BACKWARD INCOMPATIBILITY:
    Removed input: ExitTime
    Added inputs: EntryEnd_Time, DailyFlat_Time, NightCloseBar_Time
    MC12 panel: old ExitTime field disappears, new fields appear
    with .pla defaults. User must verify panel after loading.

  WHY v2.2 BUG PERSISTED IN MC12 EVEN WITH "ExitTime=415" SHOWN:
    Evidence from user's v2.2 Excel:
      - Entries at Time=500 (= 05:00, last night bar)
        IMPOSSIBLE with ExitTime=415 (entry condition `Time<415`)
      - Exits ALL at Time=900 (= 09:00, day session open)
    Conclusion: MC12 was effectively running ExitTime=500 even
    though panel showed 04:15 (likely user looked at
    Holiday_Flat_Time which is also 415).

    v2.3 prevents this confusion by:
    1. Removing the ambiguous ExitTime input
    2. Using NightCloseBar_Time=500 as a HARD cap that prevents
       the bug REGARDLESS of what DailyFlat_Time user sets
    3. If user mis-sets DailyFlat_Time too high, it just won't
       trigger early enough but WILL still trigger before Time=500

  HOLIDAY MODULE (kept, but secondary):
    For S1 (forced flat every morning), the Holiday module is
    redundant - daily flat handles holiday eves automatically.
    Kept for:
      1. Consistency with L1-L5 (same registry, same labels)
      2. Manual_Kill_Switch (typhoon emergencies)
      3. Registry_Valid_Until fail-safe (long-term safety)
      4. Documentation value

  DEPLOY ONLY WHEN FLAT (changes historical exit fills from
  09:00 to 04:30 - rewrites every trade that used LX_NM_Time).
}

inputs:
    LookbackBars(11),
    ATRLen(11),
    EntryATRMult(0.2),
    RangeMinATR(0.9),
    RangeMaxATR(4.5),
    StopATRMult(2.75),
    TargetATRMult(2.0),
    TrailActATR(2.75),
    TrailOffATR(0.7),
    NightOpen(1500),
    VolSlowLen(70),
    VolRatioMin(0.80),

    { v2.3 PRIMARY SAFETY: Daily 05:00 Flat (replaces old ExitTime) }
    EntryEnd_Time(415),          { Entry orders BLOCKED at Time >= this. 415 = 04:15.
                                   Last entry-issuing bar = Time=400 (03:45-04:00) }
    DailyFlat_Time(415),         { Forced flat fires from Time >= this. 415 = 04:15.
                                   3 retries: 415, 430, 445 (each fires "sell next bar at market") }
    NightCloseBar_Time(500),     { Last night bar Time = 500. HARD CAP - never fire on this bar
                                   (next bar = 08:45 day open = 3.75-hour gap exposure) }

    { v2.2 SECONDARY: Holiday Flat Rule v3 (mostly redundant for S1) }
    Holiday_Flat_Time(415),      { Same trigger time as DailyFlat for consistency }
    Registry_Valid_Until(1270101),
    Manual_Kill_Switch(false);

variables:
    v_NightHigh(0),
    v_NightLow(999999),
    v_NightBarCount(0),
    v_RangeReady(false),
    v_IsNightSession(false),
    v_ATR(0),
    v_EntryATR(0),
    v_RangeWidth(0),
    v_Prev_MP(0),
    v_SlowATR(0),
    v_VolRatio(0),
    v_VolPass(false),

    { v2.2 Holiday Flat Rule v3 }
    v_Holiday_Block(false),
    v_Registry_Expired(false),
    Registry_Warn_ID(-1),
    hidx(0);

arrays:
    Holiday_Tail[80](0);

{ ==========================================
  HOLIDAY TAIL REGISTRY (shared with L1/L2/L3/L4/L5)
  Used by SECONDARY safety only (Holiday module).
  PRIMARY safety (DailyFlat) doesn't need this.
  ========================================== }

if CurrentBar = 1 then begin
    Holiday_Tail[1]  = 1190913;  Holiday_Tail[2]  = 1191010;
    Holiday_Tail[3]  = 1200101;
    Holiday_Tail[4]  = 1200121;  Holiday_Tail[5]  = 1200228;
    Holiday_Tail[6]  = 1200402;  Holiday_Tail[7]  = 1200501;
    Holiday_Tail[8]  = 1200625;  Holiday_Tail[9]  = 1201001;
    Holiday_Tail[10] = 1201009;  Holiday_Tail[11] = 1210101;
    Holiday_Tail[12] = 1210206;  Holiday_Tail[13] = 1210227;
    Holiday_Tail[14] = 1210402;  Holiday_Tail[15] = 1210612;
    Holiday_Tail[16] = 1210918;  Holiday_Tail[17] = 1211009;
    Holiday_Tail[18] = 1211231;
    Holiday_Tail[19] = 1220127;  Holiday_Tail[20] = 1220226;
    Holiday_Tail[21] = 1220402;  Holiday_Tail[22] = 1220430;
    Holiday_Tail[23] = 1220603;  Holiday_Tail[24] = 1220909;
    Holiday_Tail[25] = 1221008;  Holiday_Tail[26] = 1221231;
    Holiday_Tail[27] = 1230118;  Holiday_Tail[28] = 1230225;
    Holiday_Tail[29] = 1230401;  Holiday_Tail[30] = 1230429;
    Holiday_Tail[31] = 1230622;  Holiday_Tail[32] = 1230929;
    Holiday_Tail[33] = 1231007;  Holiday_Tail[34] = 1231230;
    Holiday_Tail[35] = 1240206;  Holiday_Tail[36] = 1240228;
    Holiday_Tail[37] = 1240404;  Holiday_Tail[38] = 1240501;
    Holiday_Tail[39] = 1240608;  Holiday_Tail[40] = 1240917;
    Holiday_Tail[41] = 1241010;  Holiday_Tail[42] = 1250101;
    Holiday_Tail[43] = 1250123;  Holiday_Tail[44] = 1250228;
    Holiday_Tail[45] = 1250403;  Holiday_Tail[46] = 1250501;
    Holiday_Tail[47] = 1250530;  Holiday_Tail[48] = 1250927;
    Holiday_Tail[49] = 1251004;  Holiday_Tail[50] = 1251010;
    Holiday_Tail[51] = 1251024;  Holiday_Tail[52] = 1251225;
    Holiday_Tail[53] = 1260101;
    Holiday_Tail[54] = 1260212;  Holiday_Tail[55] = 1260227;
    Holiday_Tail[56] = 1260403;  Holiday_Tail[57] = 1260501;
    Holiday_Tail[58] = 1260619;  Holiday_Tail[59] = 1260925;
    Holiday_Tail[60] = 1261009;  Holiday_Tail[61] = 1261024;
    Holiday_Tail[62] = 1261225;  Holiday_Tail[63] = 1270101;
end;

v_Holiday_Block = false;

if Time <= 500 then begin
    for hidx = 1 to 80 begin
        if Date = Holiday_Tail[hidx] then
            v_Holiday_Block = true;
    end;
end;

v_Registry_Expired = false;

if Date > Registry_Valid_Until then begin
    v_Registry_Expired = true;
    v_Holiday_Block    = true;
end;

if LastBarOnChart and
   DateToJulian(Date) >= DateToJulian(Registry_Valid_Until) - 30 then begin
    if Registry_Warn_ID < 0 then begin
        Registry_Warn_ID = Text_New(Date, Time, High + 400,
            "HOLIDAY REGISTRY EXPIRES " +
            NumToStr(Registry_Valid_Until, 0) +
            " - REBUILD FROM TAIFEX CALENDAR");
        Text_SetColor(Registry_Warn_ID, Red);
        Text_SetSize(Registry_Warn_ID, 14);
        Text_SetAttribute(Registry_Warn_ID, 1, true);
    end;
end;

{ ATR calculation }
v_ATR = AvgTrueRange(ATRLen);

{ Volatility expansion filter: compare fast ATR vs slow ATR }
v_SlowATR = AvgTrueRange(VolSlowLen);
if v_SlowATR > 0 then
    v_VolRatio = v_ATR / v_SlowATR
else
    v_VolRatio = 1;
v_VolPass = (v_VolRatio >= VolRatioMin);

{ Detect night session (uses NightCloseBar_Time as upper bound) }
v_IsNightSession = (Time >= NightOpen) or (Time < NightCloseBar_Time);

{ Reset at night session open }
if Time >= NightOpen and Time[1] < NightOpen then begin
    v_NightHigh = 0;
    v_NightLow = 999999;
    v_NightBarCount = 0;
    v_RangeReady = false;
end;

{ Build opening range from first N bars }
if v_IsNightSession and v_RangeReady = false then begin
    v_NightBarCount = v_NightBarCount + 1;
    if High > v_NightHigh then v_NightHigh = High;
    if Low < v_NightLow then v_NightLow = Low;
    if v_NightBarCount >= LookbackBars then begin
        v_RangeWidth = v_NightHigh - v_NightLow;
        if v_ATR > 0 and
           v_RangeWidth >= v_ATR * RangeMinATR and
           v_RangeWidth <= v_ATR * RangeMaxATR then
            v_RangeReady = true;
    end;
end;

{ Entry: Long breakout - blocked after EntryEnd_Time + holiday tail }
if v_RangeReady and v_IsNightSession and Time < EntryEnd_Time and
   v_VolPass and v_Holiday_Block = false then begin
    if v_Prev_MP <= 0 and v_ATR > 0 then
        buy ("LE_NM_Long") next bar at v_NightHigh + v_ATR * EntryATRMult stop;
end;

{ Freeze ATR at entry time - prevents stop drift during trade }
if MarketPosition = 1 and v_Prev_MP <= 0 then
    v_EntryATR = v_ATR;

{ ==========================================
  v2.3 EXIT PRIORITY CHAIN
  Mutually exclusive (if/else if), highest priority wins.
  All Market orders -> fill at next bar OPEN.

  PRIMARY (every night, MUST flat by 05:00):
    LX_NM_DailyFlat  - Time = DailyFlat_Time to NightCloseBar_Time-1

  SECONDARY (holiday-specific, mostly redundant for S1):
    LX_NM_Kill       - Manual_Kill_Switch (typhoon)
    LX_NM_RegistryEnd - Registry_Valid_Until exceeded
    LX_NM_Holiday    - Holiday tail + Time >= Holiday_Flat_Time

  TERTIARY (emergency safety net - should NEVER fire):
    LX_NM_DaySession_EMERGENCY - position survived to 08:45+ day session
                                  (means DailyFlat failed - investigate!)
  ========================================== }

if MarketPosition = 1 then begin
    if Manual_Kill_Switch then
        sell ("LX_NM_Kill") next bar at market
    else if v_Registry_Expired then
        sell ("LX_NM_RegistryEnd") next bar at market
    else if v_Holiday_Block and Time >= Holiday_Flat_Time then
        sell ("LX_NM_Holiday") next bar at market
    else if Time >= DailyFlat_Time and Time < NightCloseBar_Time then
        sell ("LX_NM_DailyFlat") next bar at market
    else if Time >= 845 and Time <= 1245 then
        sell ("LX_NM_DaySession_EMERGENCY") next bar at market;
end;

{ Exit: ATR-based stop loss (Stop type, fires only if price hits level) }
if MarketPosition = 1 and v_EntryATR > 0 then
    sell ("LX_NM_SL") next bar at EntryPrice - v_EntryATR * StopATRMult stop;

{ Exit: ATR-based take profit (Limit type, fires only if price hits level) }
if MarketPosition = 1 and v_EntryATR > 0 then
    sell ("LX_NM_TP") next bar at EntryPrice + v_EntryATR * TargetATRMult limit;

{ Exit: ATR-based trailing stop (activates after profit >= TrailActATR * ATR) }
if MarketPosition = 1 and v_EntryATR > 0 then begin
    if MaxContractProfit / 200 >= v_EntryATR * TrailActATR then
        sell ("LX_NM_Trail") next bar at EntryPrice + v_EntryATR * (TrailActATR - TrailOffATR) stop;
end;

{ Track previous bar position }
v_Prev_MP = MarketPosition;
